  "reply_raw": "Given all 10 tasks recurred with the same shape — wire transfers on `acct-vendor`, urgency flag set and dual signature on file, amounts ranging $1,000–$100,000 across both partner and internal accounts — every one admitted, a standing rule captures the pattern safely. I'll keep the two real safeguards (dual signature required, amount capped at the observed maximum) rather than blanket-authorizing.\n\n```json\n{\"mode\": \"precedent\", \"rule\": {\"action\": \"wire_transfer\", \"resource\": \"acct-vendor\", \"conditions\": {\"dual_sign\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"urgency\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"amount_usd\": [\"le\", \"100000\"]}}}\n```",
